  <section class="method" id="method" aria-label="How the radar works">
    <h2>How the radar works</h2>
    <p><strong>Implied value = TVL &times; category multiple &times; growth factor
    &times; breadth factor &times; maturity factor.</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Category multiple</strong> &mdash; a per-category FDV/TVL multiple
      (Dexs 0.30, Lending 0.28, Derivatives 0.40, RWA 0.35, Chain 0.50, all others
      0.15&ndash;0.45, unlisted 0.25): what a token in that line of business has
      traded at, relative to the value locked in it.</li>
      <li><strong>Growth factor</strong> &mdash; the 7-day TVL change, clamped to
      &minus;50% &hellip; +150%. Rises are rewarded at 0.6 per point, falls punished
      at 1.0 per point. No change reported counts as flat.</li>
      <li><strong>Breadth factor</strong> &mdash; 1 + 0.04 per extra chain, up to
      six extra chains: a protocol live on more chains reaches more users.</li>
      <li><strong>Maturity factor</strong> &mdash; 0.70 + 0.30 &times; min(age, 3 years)
      / 3 years: a longer record with no token is a longer record to price.
      Age unknown counts as one year.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>What counts as pre-token.</strong> A protocol records no token when
    DefiLlama&rsquo;s record carries no market cap, no CoinGecko id and no symbol
    for it &mdash; which is not proof it has none. The board leaves out wrapped,
    staked and bridged products, centralised exchanges and versioned pools
    (the watchlist&rsquo;s rule, without its $50M floor): 40 protocols sit on the
    watchlist and 138 more below it, for 198 ranked rows.</p>
    <p><strong>Farm plans.</strong> Every row carries six steps: set up a clean
    wallet, the protocol&rsquo;s core action, a second action, a weekly action,
    checking its own points page, and holding long enough to be counted in more
    than one snapshot. Each step states what it costs and how long it takes.
    Never pay to claim anything, and claim only from links the protocol itself
    publishes.</p>
